# The tests read source, docs and generated files as text and match on literal
# `\n` boundaries (front matter fences, `export default {` blocks, the byte-for-
# byte `skills/index.json` comparison). A CRLF checkout — which `core.autocrlf=
# true` does by default on Windows — makes those checks fail against files that
# are perfectly fine in the repository. Normalise the whole tree to LF so the
# working copy matches what the tools emit and what CI sees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Kept explicit: `skills/index.json` is generated by `pnpm run skill:sync`, and
# `test/utils/skill-manifest.spec.ts` compares the checked-out file to the
# generator's output byte for byte. The generator reads `SKILL.md` frontmatter
# too, so the whole package — not just the generated JSON — has to stay LF.
skills/** text eol=lf
